      "id": "a1f0c2d3-0001-4a01-9a01-vortexnotes1",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Vortex feedback v2 → Plane\n\nSynchronous v2 + private logs. Production status: files/vortex-intake/deployment-status.md.\n\nSee files/vortex-intake/README.md for deployment, credentials, recovery and tests.\n\nSame public URL/token. JSON legacy + JSON v2; multipart payload + attachment and/or logs (bug only).\nV2: only HTTP 200 completed after issue + every file (attachment, logs) is confirmed. Legacy JSON retains early202 (no delivery guarantee).\n\nPrivate adapter uses a SQLite ledger and a single-instance lock; client retains bytes on failure.\nWebhook uses Vortex Shared Secret; adapter header X-Vortex-Intake-Token comes from $env.VORTEX_INTAKE_TOKEN.\nNever enable blind HTTP retries.\n\nTelegram: after a CONFIRMED intake, Build Telegram message → Telegram run AFTER the response to Vortex, errors ignored (they never affect the intake). The chat id (Config) and the bot credential live only in n8n, never in git; the placeholder keeps it silent.\nEmail remains disabled and disconnected.",
        "width": 720,
        "height": 420
      }
    },
